<title>USA: AEP refutes criticism of U.S. smog control efforts.</title>
<headline>AEP refutes criticism of U.S. smog control efforts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Recent criticism of Midwest electric utilities on emission controls are unfounded and may create obstacles to current efforts to restructure the electric industry, Ohio-based American Electric Power said.</p>
<p>&quot;These criticisms are advanced as environmental concerns. I'm afraid they may have more to do with some high-cost utilities in the Northeast hiding behind a kind of 'green smokescreen,'&quot; AEP executive vice president William Lhota said Friday at a Department of Energy regional meeting in Chicago.</p>
</text>
